course: dictionary
lesson: 9289
title: Meet the sparrow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sparrow is a small, common bird. It is brown and grey, and you will often see one in a garden, a park or a town. When you read about a sparrow, the words around it tell you where it lives and what it does.
explain: «Each city bird uses the city its own way: sparrows hop round the crumbs, starlings swirl over the roofs at dusk.» The words «hop round the crumbs» show what a sparrow does in a city: it hops about, looking for food on the ground.
explain: «Some are as big as a toddler, some as small as a sparrow.» Here the sentence compares sizes. A toddler is big, so a sparrow must be very small. Context clues like this help you picture a word even if you have never seen the thing itself.
fact: A sparrow is a small, common, brown and grey bird.
fact: Sparrows live near houses, gardens and towns.
fact: Sparrows eat seeds and insects.
fact: «Sparrow» is a noun: one sparrow, and many sparrows. A group of them is called a flock.
fact: The house sparrow has become rarer in some places, so it is worth noticing them in your own garden.
exercise: «Each city bird uses the city its own way: sparrows hop round the crumbs, starlings swirl over the roofs at dusk.» What do sparrows do in the city? | *Hop round the crumbs | Dig deep holes in the ground | Swim in the river | Hunt deer in the forest
exercise: Which bird is small, common, and brown and grey, living near houses and gardens? | Heron | Ostrich | *Sparrow | Eagle
exercise: «Some are as big as a toddler, some as small as a sparrow.» What does this sentence tell you about sparrows? | They wade into rivers for fish | They live in holes in the ground | They are as big as a toddler | *They are very small
test: What do sparrows eat? | Only meat from large animals | *Seeds and insects | Fish from rivers | Nectar from flowers
test: Which phrase means a group of sparrows? | A herd of cows | A pride of lions | *A flock of sparrows | A school of whales
exam: Which sentence best describes a sparrow? | A tall tree with pink flowers | A large black bird that lives in the sea | A fish that swims in rivers | *A small, common, brown and grey bird that lives near houses
